# Research Notes: NFL Injury-Report -> Line-Move Timing

Agent 15 - designation impact on market prices & optimal scrape timing
Sources: OddsIndex, Action Network, LSports, BestOdds, WagerBird, CBS Sports,
NFL.com, Rotowire, Ravens.com injury report legend. (Aug 2025-Aug 2026 cycle.)

## 1. The designations (official vs. the task's "MP")

Official NFL injury-report legend (confirmed via ravens.com/nfl.com):

Practice report (Wed/Thu/Fri cadence):
- FP  Full participation - 100% of normal reps
- LP  Limited participation - <100% of reps
- DNP Did not participate
- DNP-NIR / DNP-NI - did not participate, non-injury (rest)
- MP  NOT an official NFL designation. Aggregator code for "Mock Practice" /
      walkthrough-only (present, contact drills only, below LP). Treat as weak LP.

Game status (Fri designation for Sun games; Sat for Mon games):
- OUT      - will not play
- DOUBTFUL - unlikely to play (~25% historical play rate)
- QUESTIONABLE - uncertain (~50/50 official; ~70-75% actually play historically)
- (PROBABLE removed by the NFL in 2017.)

## 2. Which designations actually move lines

| Designation | Market impact | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| OUT (incl. 90-min inactives) | LARGE / sharp | Confirmed inactive = max repricing; biggest single driver. |
| DOUBTFUL | Moderate-to-large | Backups' value rises; reacts but w/ uncertainty. |
| QUESTIONABLE | Moderate (often mispriced) | ~70-75% play historically => market often OVERPRICES absence. Fade/public trap. |
| FP | Confirmational | Locks in availability; removes doubt. |
| LP | Small / provisional | Early signal; market prices the trajectory, not the snapshot. |
| DNP | Depends on trajectory | DNP x3 => near-certain inactive => large eventual move. |
| MP (mock/walkthrough) | Small / provisional | Weak-LP tier; early signal, not a line-driver. |

Positional spread impact for a confirmed-out starter:
- Starting QB ............ 3-7 pts (avg ~4-5; backup quality dependent)
- Elite WR1 .............. 1.5-3 pts
- Bell-cow RB (run-heavy).. 1-2.5 pts
- Starting LT (w/ good rush).. 1-3 pts
- Shutdown CB (vs pass-heavy).. 1-2 pts
- OL / most other starters .. 0.25-1 pt
(Totals: offensive star out => total drops; D star out => total may rise.)

Confirmed: QB absence is the lever. Everything else is noise unless it's a
true positional anchor (LT, elite pass rusher) AND depth behind them is thin.

## 3. Reporting + market-adjustment cadence

- Wednesday   1st practice report (late afternoon ET). First signals.
- Thursday    2nd practice report (late afternoon ET). Trend confirmation.
- Friday      3rd practice report (~4-6pm ET) + game status for Sun games.
               MOST SPREAD ADJUSTMENTS HAPPEN FRIDAY EVENING.
- Saturday    game status for Monday games (~4-5pm ET).
- Sunday     90 min pre-kickoff - official INACTIVE LIST.
             Single most active line-movement window of the week. Sharps watch live.
- Daily       reporter-sourced alerts (Schefter/Rapoport/Pelissero/Garafolo/
             Fowler) can move lines AHEAD of the Wed report (Tue "unlikely to play"
             beats Wed filing).

## 4. Market reaction speed (the edge window)

- Books react to CONFIRMED injury news within 2-3 minutes (LSports, Action Network).
- Process = Circle -> Re-open -> Price discovery:
  1. Circle: game off the board briefly (~1-2 min); books recalibrate, no bets.
  2. Re-open: new line posted (often over-corrects on star names).
  3. Price discovery: sharp money shifts line to true equilibrium.
- Unconfirmed news (early-signal stage) => little/no move, just widened risk tolerance.
- Reporter-sourced > official report for timing: a beat writer "unlikely to play"
  moves the line before the Friday designation. Walk-back risk exists.

## 5. Optimal scrape timing (vs. market adjustment)

Edge = ingest signal BEFORE the market adjusts, then capture value or confirm.

| Window | What to scrape | Market phase |
|---|---|---|
| Wed 5-7pm ET (Day -3/-2) | Wed practice report | Early-signal / widening |
| Thu 5-7pm ET (Day -2) | Thu practice report | Building concern; 2nd-day pattern is first real move trigger |
| Fri 4-7pm ET (Day -1) | Fri practice + game status | Primary reaction - scrape AS reports drop, not after |
| Fri 7-9pm ET | line ohlcv snapshot | Capture open vs close of Friday adjustment |
| Sat 4-6pm ET (Mon-game only) | Sat game status | Late scratch window for MNF |
| Sun 11:30am ET (gameday -90min) | 90-min inactives | Confirmed-status shock; sharpest, fastest move |

**Decision framework:**
- Early week (Wed/Thu): scrape for trajectory. DNP->LP->FP (up) = line baked in
  Friday; FP->LP->DNP (down) + reporter "out" => front-run Thursday move.
- Friday: scrape game-status + post-report line together. Questionable(75% play)
  => market overprices absence; if quality backup, line too far. Doubtful(25%) => lean with market.
- Sunday 90-min: scrape inactives vs last Friday line. Questionable->inactive =
  sharpest late move; act inside the 2-3 min window or it's gone.

**Pitfall:** Scraping ONLY the Friday game-status report puts you ~2-3 minutes
behind the sharpest books => post-price-discovery (re-priced) number, no value.
Real-time reporter alerts + Wed/Thu trajectory scraping beat "scrape Friday only."

## 6. Position groups that matter (scrape priority)

1. QB (starter vs backup quality)
2. Elite WR1 / TE / Bell-cow RB
3. LT / pass rush (matchup-dependent)
4. Secondary anchors vs pass-heavy offenses
5. Everything else = marginal

## 7. Source-of-truth & data providers

- Official: nfl.com/injuries; team injury-report pages; Rotowire
  practice-report.php; ESPN injuries endpoint.
- Real-time reporter alerts (beat official report): Schefter, Rapoport,
  Pelissero, Garafolo, Fowler - scrape their X/Twitter or a wire feed.
- Line + market-reaction timing: sportsbook APIs / LSports Scouts Feed /
  SpankOdds injury alerts.

## 8. Caveats / issues encountered

- "MP" is NOT an official NFL designation - do not expect it on the official
  Ravens/NFL legends. It is an aggregator/walkthrough code; map it to "weak LP."
- No single public source publishes exact second-level scrape-vs-line-move data;
  "2-3 min" and "Friday evening" figures are industry-reported estimates.
- "Questionable" play-rate (~70-75% actually play) is the highest-leverage stat:
  it's why the market MOVES on Friday but often OVERREACTS, which the scraper
  front-runs.
